These fields describe our own toolchain and the extraction coordinates; they
contain no firmware content. Re-verify them against the revisions actually used
for a given run before treating a contract as authoritative.

## Extraction coordinates (verified)

For an ELF32 ARM binary whose `.text` maps `vaddr 0x15710 -> file offset 0x5710`,
the file offset of the region is:

```python
file_offset = symbol_vaddr + text_file_offset - text_vaddr   # 0x101aac + 0x5710 - 0x15710 = 0xf1aac
```

The first three words at that offset are `0xe51b24a8`-style little-endian ARM
words whose byte signature is `10 48 2d e9 08 b0 8d e2 d4 d0 4d e2`, i.e.
`STMFD SP!, {...}` / `LDR R8, [SP,#imm]` / `ADD R8, SP, #imm` — the documented
#251 prologue. Confirm this signature before trusting any extracted blob.

## Source binary (retained)

The region is extracted from `pgphoto.stage2ondisk` of firmware **6.0.0.54.90**
(`o-v18m-k1ii-pgphoto-readiness-20261029`, patcher ref `f344e41/main`,
libgphoto2 `63a894b0821a510fc40244c5cc4ef84a5220a91c`).

| field | value |
|---|---|
| source binary SHA-256 | `8973d9486e0207446cc111234ed39e878676ce1f3edca2967a97db86c8d9eaac` |
| retained at | `PrivateResearch firmware-packets/6.0.0.54.90--o-v18m-k1ii-pgphoto-readiness-20261029/extracted_appfs/stage2-ondisk/ondisk/pgphoto.stage2ondisk` |
| durable packet | `.../FwPkt.zip` (LFS-tracked, zip MD5 `4c005b0acf50676fa7e1d32ffbac9cd6`) |

Re-derivation is verified: extracting offset `0xf1aac` for 2176 bytes from the
retained copy yields this region's SHA-256 exactly.

An earlier revision of this file stated the source binary was not retained
anywhere on the host. That was wrong — a search-scope error (the build tree
`/home/ian/polaris-build-73/out/` was not searched, and it is gitignored in that
repository). The copy under `out/` is still volatile, which is why the retained
copy above exists.

## Why this region is not the stock build

Extracting the same symbol at the same address and size from the retained stock
baseline (`pgphoto.stock`, Benro 4.0.0.32, SHA-256
`0308393632dd41d974bd1064e61942655131fe5392959a334cf24623d1bd4a62`) yields region
SHA-256 `333a3f669734459807c0dc601af6f9dad1d857a51acf546da1210bd5461f7f19`. The
prologue is identical but the body differs, so the pinned blob is the patched
o-v18m build rather than stock. This is expected, not a defect.

## Resolved external call targets

All 42 BL sites were resolved from the retained ELF — 10 via `.symtab` FUNC
entries, 3 via `.rel.plt` → `.dynsym`:

| callee | stub group | sites |
|---|---|---|
| `gp_log` | libgphoto | 11 |
| `HI_LOG_Print` | os | 11 |
| `sqrt` (PLT) | os | 4 |
| `setCameraStatus` | camera | 2 |
| `wait_and_handle_event` | camera | 2 |
| `cb_arg_run` | callback | 2 |
| `timediff_now` | timer | 2 |
| `textdomain` (PLT) | os | 2 |
| `isatty` (PLT) | os | 2 |
| `waitCameraIdle` | camera | 1 |
| `numOfCaptureImage` | camera | 1 |
| `getImageToBuffer` | camera | 1 |
| `delayTime` | timer | 1 |

These are recorded in `stage2_region.json` as `stub_entries`, using
`"model": "call-site"` because the intercepted address is the `BL` instruction
inside the mapped blob; the callee bodies lie outside the extracted window.

## Lifecycle vocabulary mismatch

None of the 13 callees is named `stop`, `close`, `cancel`, `message_stop` or
`context_cancel`, yet those are what the nine lifecycle cases assert on. The
owners are elsewhere in the same binary:

| symbol | address | size | called from |
|---|---|---|---|
| `stopCaptureImageForMessage` | `0x202e4` | 108 | `captureBulbImage`, `sonyBurstEvent` |
| `stopCaptureContinuContinuous` | `0x20350` | 156 | — |
| `captureBulbImage` | `0x20604` | 684 | — |
| `gp_context_cancel` | `0x358d0` | 104 | 27 libgphoto call sites |
| `gp_camera_stop_timeout` | `0x35158` | 476 | `gp_camera_exit` |

So the message-driven stop edge is owned by `stopCaptureImageForMessage`,
reached from `captureBulbImage` — not by `capture_image_with_Bulb`. Testing
those edges needs its own pinned region (see harness issue #19).

## Retrieval procedure (private research repo only)

The binary region must NOT be committed to this public repository. To obtain
it locally:

1. In the private research repo, locate `pgphoto.stage2ondisk` from the
   v90-era firmware build.
2. Extract the region at address `0x101aac`, length `2176` bytes.
3. Verify SHA-256: `23398c6efc7c737c1b2b91664a98b45a2b7bc01f97e704c3ccb4bf3fc4a618c3`
4. Place the extracted binary as `tests/fixtures/arm/stage2_region.bin`
   (locally only — do NOT commit).
5. Create the sidecar `tests/fixtures/arm/stage2_region.json` declaring how to
   execute it. Without this the region is decoded as Thumb at `0x1000` and
   faults on instruction one, and external calls run as real code instead of
   reaching stubs:

   ```json
   {
     "description": "capture_image_with_Bulb region, v90-era",
     "source_issue": "ian-morgan99/benro-polaris-firmware-patcher#251",
     "provenance": {
       "type": "extracted-private",
       "mode": "arm",
       "entry_address": "0x101aac",
       "code_address": "0x101aac",
       "code_size": 65536,
       "max_instructions": 200000,
       "stub_entries": [
         {"address": "<stop target>", "stub_name": "camera",
          "function_name": "stop", "model": "target"},
         {"address": "<close target>", "stub_name": "camera",
          "function_name": "close", "model": "target"}
       ]
     }
   }
   ```

   `code_address` must contain the entry address and every stub entry address.
   Stub targets are the PLT-style callee addresses; use `"model": "target"` for
   them, or `"call-site"` if you register the `BL` instruction itself instead.
   The lifecycle assertions filter on `function_name`, so declare one per entry.
6. Update this placeholder with patcher commit, harness revision, emulator
   version, fixture/stub profile, and command.
7. Run `polaris-harness arm-emulate --suite`. With the region present the nine
   cases execute it in ARM mode; a behavioural failure exits 3.

A committed, firmware-free example of a correctly annotated fixture is
`tests/fixtures/arm/lifecycle_probe_fixture.{bin,json}`.

## Constraints (from issue #15)

- Never patch or mutate the input artifact.
- Bind every run to input binary SHA-256, patcher commit, harness revision,
  emulator version, fixture/stub profile, command, and full machine-readable result.
- Fail closed on unknown binary hashes/layouts.
- The binary must NOT be published on GitHub — retrieval is local only.
